      "usefulness": "Codemagic v3 user, team, app, and build reads provide cheap authenticated CI inventory without triggering billed builds.",
      "incident": "5 December 2022 Codemagic disclosed a misconfigured Google Cloud bucket that allowed unauthorized listing of about 140TB / 31 million objects (build artifacts, Linux/Windows cache, logs, write-only upload credentials, avatars). User passwords and source code were not stored there. Bucket listing was closed the same day; logs were moved by 6 December 2022.",
      "remediation": "Bucket permissions were tightened on 5 December 2022, internal upload credentials were rotated, logs were migrated to a new bucket, and later artifact URLs gained expiration. This is historical and remediated, not a current unresolved API-key compromise.",
